# Build context hygiene. The context is the repo root (the uv workspace lock spans every
# member), so without this file `docker build` uploads .git, both virtualenvs and
# node_modules — on the 4GB VPS in DEPLOYMENT §2 that is the difference between a build
# and an OOM.
#
# ALLOW-LIST DISCIPLINE FOR SECRETS. `.env*` is excluded here as well as in .gitignore
# because the two files answer different questions: .gitignore keeps a secret out of the
# repo, .dockerignore keeps one that is sitting in the working directory on the VPS out
# of an image layer. The deploy runs in `/var/www/calevate`, where the real `.env` lives
# (DEPLOYMENT §6 tier 1) — so this line is not theoretical.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git
.github
.venv
.uv-python
node_modules
**/node_modules
apps/web/.next
apps/web/out

__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.import_linter_cache
.grimp_cache
*.egg-info

# Test and tooling trees. The runtime image runs no tests; shipping them would put
# fixtures (including transcript fixtures) into a production layer.
tests
**/*_test.py
htmlcov
.coverage
.coverage-run.json
coverage_baseline.json

docs
infra
*.md
!README.md

# `runbooks/` IS SHIPPED, and it is the one documentation tree that is (D-499). The admin
# copilot's `search_runbooks` tool reads these 22 files at RUNTIME to answer "what do I do
# when `engine_error_spike` fires" — so excluding them made that tool pass every test and
# return nothing in production, which is why `Dockerfile` copies them.
#
# THIS LINE USED TO SAY `runbooks` AND THE DEPLOY FAILED ON IT: the `COPY runbooks
# runbooks` added for that tool could not resolve, because a path excluded here is not in
# the build context at all — `docker build` fails with "/runbooks: not found" rather than
# silently shipping an empty directory. 416K, against the 5.5MB `docs` tree that stays
# excluded because nothing reads it at runtime.
#
# `*.md` above does not re-exclude them: .dockerignore patterns use Go filepath.Match, so
# `*` does not cross a `/` and that rule only matches .md files at the ROOT.

dump.rdb
*.log
*.err
*.pdf
